  "reservable": true,
  "reviews": [
    {
      "author_name": "Anil Singh",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114814427210259074301/reviews",
      "language": "en",
      "original_language": "en",
      "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVmlBS5GvLVZijVqgHAC1rdCMJSoMNex2xo27RXR3D0eotnjrf1dw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
      "rating": 5,
      "relative_time_description": "in the last week",
      "text": "In a neighborhood with tons of dining choices, try this! I especially enjoyed the Beef Chow Fun with brown sauce. The baked fried rice is awesome, but expect to wait about ten minutes for this. We also enjoyed the beef fried rice and Singapore noodles with shrimp. The waiter was very helpful with suggestions for our order. Highly recommend!",
      "time": 1750555353,
      "translated": false
    },
    {
      "author_name": "the bb",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106373354159261409961/reviews",
      "language": "en",
      "original_language": "en",
      "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJPdvJxcLJv6pBVi3A8j10VfYtgiwkWDG7XEvKWxvLp612oefJM=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
      "rating": 4,
      "relative_time_description": "a month ago",
      "text": "Tasty comfort food. Kitchen was sold out of some stuff already even though we weren’t there that late so didn’t get to try the rice rolls. Unexpectedly really liked the baked rice w chicken Portuguese style. Other highlights were the Fries, Golden lava French toast and chow fun.",
      "time": 1748142507,
      "translated": false
    },
    {
      "author_name": "Ana Zheng",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101134176142540180863/reviews",
      "language": "en",
      "original_language": "en",
      "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVXtGjHOVYYdrrFPhvoCH_1a6zybG1yaeMfQGClEO3p8YiZWah36w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
      "rating": 5,
      "relative_time_description": "2 weeks ago",
      "text": "wow — what an unforgettable experience! I stumbled upon this spot and decided to try something different: French toast and pesto pasta. I wasn’t expecting much, but both dishes completely blew me away!\n\nThe French toast was soft on the inside, crispy on the outside, and perfectly sweet — honestly some of the best I’ve had. But the real surprise was the pesto pasta. I didn’t think I’d find amazing pasta in Chinatown, but it was SO good! Creamy, flavorful, and cooked just right.\n\nEverything was super affordable too, which made the whole experience even better. It’s hard to find good quality food at a low price in NYC, but this place nailed it.\n\nIf it’s your first time in Chinatown, definitely give this place a try — the food is cheap, delicious, and way better than I expected. I’m already planning to come back and try more dishes. A hidden gem for sure!",
      "time": 1749442307,
      "translated": false
    },
    {
      "author_name": "Fahim Shariar",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107754217527403864184/reviews",
      "language": "en",
      "original_language": "en",
      "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVjbn2nVy0tQYUMSqotZ59ess8A4xz7-zIVrjmmu8WklN8rbE7Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
      "rating": 5,
      "relative_time_description": "3 weeks ago",
      "text": "If you’re in china town, this is the place to be!\n\nI had an amazing experience here. Everything had immense flavor. Service was phenomenal, our waiter (the one with the Mohawk) was very attentive and friendly. Food came out faster than expected as well.\n\nI’d recommend steam dumplings, French toast & of course chicken chop with baked rice.",
      "time": 1749338182,
      "translated": false
    },
    {
      "author_name": "Xin",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115499328070754850684/reviews",
      "language": "en",
      "original_language": "en",
      "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXjMx0oceFkfDk2M_NiYYuKNzU8oJDZJKDh-mAWmGHwZx1uVfiq=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
      "rating": 5,
      "relative_time_description": "a month ago",
      "text": "YUM! This is the spot for HK style cafe food. The noodle and curry are delicious and reasonably priced, the drinks are good, and the staff are friendly. Not pictured is house special fried rice which I also highly recommend. Bring cash.",
